What that record covers, said exactly. On the .NET side it covers the package
and project references written literally in the project files of
the three projects that ship in this package: Semanticus.Core,
Semanticus.Analysis and Semanticus.Engine. It reads project text, not a build.
Nothing is evaluated: no MSBuild import is read as a source of references, no
property is expanded beyond a single unconditioned definition in the same file,
no condition is evaluated, and no claim is made about which of those references
a build actually copies into the payload.

It is therefore not the resolved publish closure. These sit outside it: the
transitive packages those references pull in, the .NET 8 runtime pack that the
self-contained publish copies into the payload, and anything a transitive pulls
in turn. Deriving that closure is the named open item, tracked on the project
board and disclosed in the "Exactly what it does NOT do" section of
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Read that section before relying on this one.
